# An allow-list: the build context is the repo root, so everything is excluded unless a
# Dockerfile needs it. A new config or secret file therefore cannot reach an image by accident.
# When the server gains a path dependency, add it here and to dev.Dockerfile.dockerignore as well
# as to its pyproject.toml.
*

!apps/server/
!packages/proto/
!packages/organization-info/
!packages/core-domain/
!buf.yaml
!buf.gen.python.yaml
!buf.gen.server.yaml
!scripts/generate_proto.py

# Re-excluded inside the allowed paths: host-built or host-specific state. Unlike the dev image,
# generated code stays out: this image generates its own.
**/.venv
**/gen
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.private.*
**/*.local.*
**/private
**/.env
**/.env.*
